        "note": "SVG files"
      },
      {
        "pathPattern": ".*[.](ya?ml|json|jsonc|xml|toml|ini|cfg|conf|properties|plist|webmanifest)",
        "contentPattern": "",
        "exception": false,
        "note": "Configuration and non-build markup - OUT (scope policy sec.3). This is the rule that closes the 7,500 LOC/PY default over-valuation by SCOPE rather than by rate (MC-dvvjijla, 2026-07-12). READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING IT ONLY AFFECTS MAIN. CodeConfiguration.updateScopesFiles removes 'other' from test and from buildAndDeployment as well as from main, so a file this rule matches leaves EVERY other scope. Verified against the shipped JAR: src/test/resources/*.xml and *.yaml land in other, not test, and pom.xml lands in other, not buildAndDeployment. Test LOC therefore shrinks too, and test LOC feeds TEST_VS_MAIN_LINES_OF_CODE_PERCENTAGE, which the active calibration scores - so this rule moves a score through TEST_RATIO as well as through volume, and not always in the same direction. Measured: mc-quality-engine's test LOC falls 4,783 to 4,770 and its maintainability falls 3.7701 to 3.7697. Whether to spare test-scope files via an `exception` rule is an open decision, not an oversight (MC-enutgcnt code review F3)."
      },
      {
        "pathPattern": ".*[.](md|markdown|rst|rest|adoc|asciidoc|txt)",
        "contentPattern": "",
        "exception": false,
        "note": "Documentation and prose markup - OUT (scope policy sec.3, end-user/operator documentation). The standard set ignores a docs/ FOLDER by path; this catches prose that lives outside one, which is most of it. Also catches the git-*.txt sidecars extractGitHistory writes into the work tree, whose standard ignore rules the shipped JAR does not all match."
      }
    ],
    "files": []
  },
